# Doctoral Program AI Governance & Syllabus Modernization Framework
**Context:** Executive Doctoral Program Administration & Higher Education AI Policy  
**Institutional Alignment:** Belhaven University, St. Petersburg College (SPC), Eastern University  
**Case Study Focus:** BUS 700 Orientation Seminar Syllabus Modernization[cite: 7]  
**Author:** Securiti Certified AI Security & Governance Specialist & Executive Faculty  

---

## 1. Executive Summary & Policy Context
As generative AI reshapes graduate education, doctoral programs require transparent governance frameworks that preserve academic rigor, protect data privacy, and establish evidence of authentic student learning[cite: 1]. This case study modernizes the BUS 700 Orientation Seminar syllabus by integrating Belhaven University's official *Faculty Guidance for Responding to AI Detection Scores* protocol[cite: 1, 7]. The policy operates on a foundational guiding principle: **AI detection tools (e.g., Turnitin) prompt faculty inquiry rather than serve as definitive proof of academic misconduct**[cite: 1].

